    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.41), whose favorable matchup against Lowder (4.84 xERA) makes him our strongest offensive asset, closely followed by **Kyle Tucker** (71.81) and **Miguel Vargas** (66.32). **Vargas** earns a significant boost today by batting leadoff against Quintana, where the high-upside environment, combined with the pitcher's slow delivery, makes him a primary target for our stolen base objectives. Meanwhile, **Henry Bolte** (65.23) is a dark horse play; he benefits from a massive 10% park factor adjustment and a prime spot at the top of the order, effectively neutralizing any platoon concerns against Wesneski. **Jackson Merrill** (65.51) also profiles as a high-floor start, as his platoon advantage against Clarke provides the necessary efficiency to stay well above our 60-point threshold for strong starts.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Wade Meckler** (36.86), who failed to clear our 40-point \"zebra\" floor. Despite his contact profile, his L/L platoon disadvantage against Anderson and a poor park factor caused his score to plummet, keeping him sidelined in favor of higher-ceiling options like **Nasim Nunez**, whose speed potential and favorable matchup against Tong keep him in the lineup despite a lower base projection. We remain vigilant regarding the health of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** as they continue their stints on the IL, while **Gunnar Henderson** sits today due to a team off-day. With the league\u2019s stolen base scarcity in mind, we are leaning heavily into the speed profiles of **Miguel Vargas** and **Andy Pages** to bridge the gap in our 5x5 Roto standings during this final week of the season.",
